{"metabox":"1","type":"annotation","subject":"crates/path-cli/src/projection/copilot.rs","issuer":"mailto:1240090+bdelanghe@users.noreply.github.com","issuer_type":"ai","created_at":"2026-10-15T18:25:10.606929Z","id":"02583de7580c52a61802994b76cfb2f05390a71a26b19f7b6b2c231ca6b316d0","body":{"detail":"Round robin: claude, codex and pi keep the source session id through every hop; copilot -> * returns a new id (a1539809..., 87c5973f..., ...). If copilot accepts an arbitrary UUID as a session id, reuse view.id as the other projectors do; if not, record the mapping in meta so the identity is recoverable. review/roundrobin.md, 2026-10-15.","kind":"concern","span":{"start":{"line":6},"end":{"line":6},"content_hash":"d39eb5434060b5d941878a6b9f77e819e87052ced17a47dd41b47547b884662d"},"summary":"a copilot projection always mints a fresh session id, so copilot is the one hop that loses the session identity","tags":["review","roundtrip","defect-candidate","session:claude-code:7c8ae6d3-afd1-4605-913b-9fd31e45468f"]}}
